  pages     = {1--7},
  year      = {2025},
  abstract  = {This work analyzes sea-surface-height reflectometry using multi-observation information from BDS signals. It evaluates station geometry, reflection zones, satellite tracks, and retrieval accuracy, and compares different observation combinations for sea-level monitoring. The results support the use of BDS-based reflectometry as a practical approach for coastal water-level and sea-surface-height applications.},
